## Actual-response text-guard follow-up (provider.py only)

The controller reproduced rejection on the exact archived runtime/controller-investigator-round1-response.json: causal_claim contains the normal sentence “A plausible cause ...”, and author_instructions contains “no I/O”. Source reading confirms the uppercase regex treats bare A, I and O as unknown uppercase symbols. No synthetic inputs or application calls were used by this implementer.

Added bare A and I to the existing ordinary-uppercase token allowance. Added recognition of bounded exact I/O only in the uppercase scan, by masking its three characters locally. Boundaries exclude embedding in identifiers, slash/dot paths, dollar prefixes and dotted alphanumeric suffixes. The original text still goes through path, credential and explicit ticker-context scans first; the original text is returned unchanged, so stored text/hash is unchanged. Cash and market suffix checks still run and reject A/I with those markers; standalone O and other unknown uppercase tokens remain rejected. No other parser or role schema changed.

provider.py was snapshotted with exact original bytes and added to the eight-file inventories and patch. The seven previously proposed wiring hashes are unchanged, recorded in seven-wiring-hashes-before-provider-fix.json; the ongoing wiring review therefore remains against the same bytes. All eight proposed files compile and Ruff passes. All eight live source files still match their preimages. This module is evaluator-covered and must be included in later rebuild identity. The controller will preflight the exact archived response only after safe application; this report does not claim that execution has occurred. No live source, tests, probes, network, Docker, credentials or commits touched.
